---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `My phone tells me I used it for some huge number of minutes
this week and I have no idea whether that is bad. Turn it
into hours and minutes, and tell me the daily average too.`;

const Sample = `Minutes this week: 1147 [Enter]

That is 19 hours and 7 minutes.
Daily average: 2 hours and 43 minutes.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/unit-1/cc-set-1" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 1
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Screen Time</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> What
            goes in, what gets worked out, what comes out, and{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">every question the brief did not
            answer.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Hours and minutes out of a single number is a division and a remainder. You have both.</li>
            <li><b>Lua's <code>/</code> never truncates</b>, so <code>1147 / 60</code> is not 19. Session 5 has the fix.</li>
            <li>The daily average has the same shape as the first answer. If you find yourself writing it twice, that is a hint about session 21 &mdash; but do it twice for now.</li>
            <li>A remainder of 0 should read sensibly. Check it.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="success">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={Sample}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3"><b>Test 60, 59, and 1440.</b> One of those three shows up a rounding decision you have not made yet.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program folder, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-screen-time</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
